md`# brain-loop

A Cloud Brain recipe with no model and no timer: told of each change to the tracker, it starts the worker machine when an issue is doable and the machine is stopped. The machine runs \`cloud-brain-dev/drain.ts\`, which ends when no issue is doable, and the machine stops with it. The switch is the setting \`on\`, the checkbox below. The design is comment 7379 of the issue \`fly-loop-needs-cloud-brain-dev-alone\`: the owner's "a decoupled service that uses issues and fly service", "no crons, should be event driven from issues, maybe via subscription to topic" (2026-10-14).

The panel under this text is for the owner, signed in.`
// %%
viewof loopView = loopPanel({ client, owner: !!(session && session.owner) })
// %%
md`## Methods

| Method | Who | What |
|---|---|---|
| \`POST loop.receive\` | the owner, a token of his, and a push of \`brain-x-topic\` under a delegation of his | The target of a subscription to the topic the tracker appends to. The body, an entry, is not read: it says that something changed. Then as \`loop.check\` |
| \`POST loop.check\` | the same | Decides now (below) and answers what \`loop.status\` answers |
| \`GET loop.status\` | the same | \`{ on, last }\`: the setting, and the last decision as \`{ at, by, doable, machine, held, did, why, error }\` |
| \`GET loop.work\` | the same | \`{ work: [{ id, about, title }] }\`: the doable issues, oldest first, by the rule \`loopDoable\` |

The rule of all four is \`caller.id == "owner"\`. A member, another Worker and anyone else are refused.

## Doable

\`loopDoable\`: an issue of \`issue.list?state=ready\` whose \`about\` is a service, \`brain-x-…\`, other than the owner's four (kernel, core, database, deployer), with none of the labels \`major\`, \`needs-owner\`, \`laptop\`, \`digest\`, \`run-stopped\`. \`laptop\` is an issue that needs what a machine does not hold; \`run-stopped\` is put by \`run.ts\` on an issue it gave back. The same rule is written in \`cloud-brain-dev/drain.ts\` (\`doable\`), which the machine runs.

## The decision

| \`on\` | doable | the machine (\`fly.status\`) | does |
|---|---|---|---|
| not true | any | \`started\` | \`fly.down\`: asks the drain to yield. The Fly service stops it later |
| not true | any | anything else | nothing |
| true | none | any | nothing: a drain that finds none ends, and the machine with it |
| true | some | none named, or not \`stopped\` | nothing |
| true | some | \`stopped\`, \`loop\` held | nothing: another loop has the tracker |
| true | some | \`stopped\`, \`loop\` not held | \`fly.up\` |

\`fly.up\` keeps the day's limit (\`maxHoursADay\` of \`brain-x-fly\`): past it the answer is 409, kept as the decision's \`error\`. Each decision is the row \`last\` and one log line \`{ at: "loop.decide", by, on, doable, machine, did, why }\`.

## Set up, the owner's

The panel's **Connect to the tracker** makes, in the owner's own session, what the push needs: the topic \`issues\` (\`topic.create\`, write \`caller.id == "worker:brain-x-issues"\`, read \`caller.id == "owner"\`), a delegation for \`brain-x-topic\` to call \`loop.receive\` (and \`quota.get\`, which a subscribe asks for), the subscription \`loop\` to the topic, and the setting \`topic\` of \`brain-x-issues\`, which makes the tracker append. The machine and its secrets are the Fly service's panel's.`
// %%
loopDefaults = ({ not: ["major", "needs-owner", "laptop", "digest", "run-stopped"], owners: ["brain-x-kernel", "brain-x-core", "brain-x-db", "brain-x-deployer"], topic: "issues" })
// %%
// The issues a machine can do, oldest first.
loopDoable = (issues) =>
  (Array.isArray(issues) ? issues : [])
    .filter((i) => i && i.state === "ready" && typeof i.about === "string" && /^brain-x-[a-z0-9-]+$/.test(i.about) && !loopDefaults.owners.includes(i.about))
    .filter((i) => !(Array.isArray(i.labels) ? i.labels : []).some((l) => loopDefaults.not.includes(l)))
    .sort((a, b) => (a.opened_at || 0) - (b.opened_at || 0) || String(a.id).localeCompare(String(b.id)))
// %%
// What a decision does: { do: "up" | "down" | null, why }. No I/O: the table of "The decision".
loopPlan = ({ on, doable, machine, held }) => {
  if (!on) return machine === "started" ? { do: "down", why: "off, and the machine runs" } : { do: null, why: "off" };
  if (!doable) return { do: null, why: "no work" };
  if (!machine) return { do: null, why: "no machine is named" };
  if (machine !== "stopped") return { do: null, why: "the machine is " + machine };
  if (held) return { do: null, why: "loop is held by " + held };
  return { do: "up", why: doable + " doable" };
}
// %%
loopOps = {
  const said = (e) => String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 200);
  const isOn = () => config.on === true || config.on === "true";
  const work = async () => loopDoable((await xrpc.query("com.lopecode.brain.issue.list", { state: "ready", limit: "500" })).issues);
  const decide = async (by, now = Date.now()) => {
    const last = { at: now, by, doable: null, machine: null, held: null, did: null, why: "", error: null };
    try {
      const ids = (await work()).map((i) => i.id), fly = await xrpc.query("com.lopecode.brain.fly.status", {});
      Object.assign(last, { doable: ids.length, machine: fly.machine ? fly.machine.state : null, held: fly.loop || null });
      const plan = loopPlan({ on: isOn(), doable: ids.length, machine: last.machine, held: last.held });
      last.why = plan.why;
      if (plan.do === "up") await xrpc.procedure("com.lopecode.brain.fly.up", {});
      if (plan.do === "down") await xrpc.procedure("com.lopecode.brain.fly.down", {});
      last.did = plan.do;
    } catch (e) {
      last.error = said(e);
    }
    await rows.put("last", last);
    log({ at: "loop.decide", by, on: isOn(), doable: last.doable, machine: last.machine, did: last.did, why: last.why, ...(last.error ? { error: last.error } : {}) });
    return last;
  };
  const status = async () => ({ on: isOn(), last: (await rows.get("last")) || null });
  return { work, decide, status };
}
// %%
loop_service = cloudflare.Service(
  "loop",
  async (request) => {
    const json = (status, body) => new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    const what = new URL(request.url).pathname.split(".").pop();
    const verb = { receive: "POST", check: "POST", status: "GET", work: "GET" }[what];
    if (!verb) return json(404, { error: "MethodNotImplemented", message: "loop.receive, loop.check, loop.status and loop.work" });
    if (request.method !== verb) return json(405, { error: "InvalidRequest", message: "loop." + what + " is sent with " + verb });
    try {
      if (what === "work") return json(200, { work: (await loopOps.work()).map((i) => ({ id: i.id, about: i.about, title: String(i.title || "").slice(0, 200) })) });
      if (what === "status") return json(200, await loopOps.status());
      await loopOps.decide(what);
      return json(200, await loopOps.status());
    } catch (e) {
      return json(502, { error: "UpstreamFailure", message: String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 300) });
    }
  },
  {
    calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.issue.list", "com.lopecode.brain.fly.status", "com.lopecode.brain.fly.up", "com.lopecode.brain.fly.down"],
    methods: {
      "com.lopecode.brain.loop.receive": { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.id == "owner"' },
      "com.lopecode.brain.loop.check": { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.id == "owner"' },
      "com.lopecode.brain.loop.status": { type: "query", allow: 'caller.id == "owner"' },
      "com.lopecode.brain.loop.work": { type: "query", allow: 'caller.id == "owner"' }
    }
  }
)
// %%
loop_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", loop_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced loop_service";
}
// %%
// The switch, what was last decided, the doable issues, and Connect.
loopPanel = ({ client, owner = false } = {}) => {
  const muted = "color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)";
  if (!client || !owner) return Object.assign(htl.html`<i style=${muted}>Sign in to a Brain as the owner to see its loop.</i>`, { value: null });
  const el = Object.assign(htl.html`<div></div>`, { value: null }), state = htl.html`<div style="margin:6px 0"></div>`;
  const note = htl.html`<pre style="${muted};margin-top:6px;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere"></pre>`;
  const said = (e) => String((e && e.message) || e);
  const box = htl.html`<input type=checkbox>`;
  const toggle = htl.html`<label style="display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;margin:6px 0">${box} Wake the worker machine when an issue is doable</label>`;
  let busy = false;
  const draw = async () => {
    let s = null, w = null, error = null;
    try {
      [s, w] = await Promise.all([client.query("loop.status"), client.query("loop.work")]);
    } catch (e) {
      error = said(e);
    }
    el.value = s;
    el.dispatchEvent(new Event("input"));
    if (!s) return void state.replaceChildren("loop.status: " + error);
    box.checked = !!s.on;
    const l = s.last, ids = (w.work || []).map((i) => i.id);
    state.replaceChildren(
      `${ids.length} doable${ids.length ? ": " + ids.join(", ") : ""}. `,
      l ? `Last decided ${new Date(l.at).toISOString()} (${l.by}): ${l.did || "nothing"}, ${l.why}${l.error ? "; " + l.error : ""}.` : "Nothing decided yet."
    );
  };
  const act = async (what, fn) => {
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    box.disabled = true;
    try {
      note.textContent = what + "…";
      note.textContent = (await fn()) || "";
    } catch (e) {
      note.textContent = `${what} failed: ${said(e)}`;
    }
    busy = false;
    box.disabled = false;
    await draw();
  };
  box.addEventListener("input", (e) => {
    e.stopPropagation();
    const on = box.checked;
    act(on ? "On" : "Off", async () => {
      await client.procedure("config.set", { worker: "brain-x-loop", key: "on", value: on });
      const s = await client.procedure("loop.check", {});
      return s.last ? `${s.last.did || "nothing"}: ${s.last.why}${s.last.error ? "; " + s.last.error : ""}` : "";
    });
  });
  // The four acts of the push, each the owner's own session's. A topic that is there already is said and kept.
  const connect = Inputs.button("Connect to the tracker", {
    reduce: () =>
      act("Connect", async () => {
        const t = loopDefaults.topic, done = [];
        try {
          await client.procedure("topic.create", { topic: t, write: 'caller.id == "worker:brain-x-issues"', read: 'caller.id == "owner"' });
          done.push("topic " + t);
        } catch (e) {
          done.push("topic " + t + ": " + said(e));
        }
        const { id } = await client.procedure("delegation.create", { name: "loop-push", holder: { worker: "brain-x-topic" }, scope: ["com.lopecode.brain.loop.receive", "com.lopecode.brain.quota.get"], note: "brain-topic pushes the tracker's changes to loop.receive" });
        done.push("delegation " + id);
        await client.procedure("topic.subscribe", { topic: t, name: "loop", target: "com.lopecode.brain.loop.receive", delegation: id });
        done.push("subscription loop");
        await client.procedure("config.set", { worker: "brain-x-issues", key: "topic", value: t });
        done.push("brain-x-issues appends to " + t);
        return done.join("\n");
      })
  });
  connect.addEventListener("input", (e) => e.stopPropagation());
  el.append(toggle, state, connect, note);
  el.ready = draw();
  return el;
}
// %%
md`## Tests

The service runs here as the emitted Worker. The tracker's \`issue.list\` and the Fly service are answers the test gives.`
// %%
// A Brain with a tracker and a Fly service as the test says. `asked` is each call the Worker made.
loopRig = async ({ on = true, issues = [], machine = "stopped", held = null, up = 200 } = {}) => {
  const asked = [], rows = new Map();
  const rig = { asked, rows, issues, fly: { machine, held } };
  rig.sim = await simulate(loop_service, {
    rows,
    config: { on },
    secrets: { BRAIN_KEY: "k" },
    core: async (request) => {
      const u = new URL(request.url), nsid = u.pathname.replace("/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.", "");
      asked.push(nsid);
      if (nsid === "issue.list") return Response.json({ issues: rig.issues, total: rig.issues.length, more: false });
      if (nsid === "fly.status") return Response.json({ app: "cloudbrain", machine: rig.fly.machine ? { id: "m1", state: rig.fly.machine } : null, loop: rig.fly.held });
      if (nsid === "fly.up") return up === 200 ? ((rig.fly.machine = "starting"), Response.json({ started: true, state: "starting" })) : Response.json({ error: "Conflict", message: "the day's limit is reached" }, { status: up });
      if (nsid === "fly.down") return Response.json({ state: "started", yield: 1 });
      return Response.json({ error: "MethodNotImplemented" }, { status: 501 });
    }
  });
  rig.call = async (name, verb = ["status", "work"].includes(name) ? "GET" : "POST") => {
    const r = await rig.sim.fetch("https://loop.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.loop." + name, { method: verb, headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "delegation:d1", "x-brain-holder": "worker:brain-x-topic", "x-brain-tab": "0" }, ...(verb === "GET" ? {} : { body: '{"seq":1}' }) });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json() };
  };
  return rig;
}
// %%
loopIssue = (id, more = {}) => ({ id, state: "ready", about: "brain-x-git", labels: [], opened_at: 1, title: id, ...more })
// %%
test_loop_doable_is_ready_a_service_not_the_owners_and_no_held_label = {
  const all = [
    loopIssue("b", { opened_at: 2 }),
    loopIssue("a", { opened_at: 2 }),
    loopIssue("first", { opened_at: 1 }),
    loopIssue("in-review", { state: "in-review" }),
    loopIssue("no-about", { about: null }),
    loopIssue("a-seed", { about: "lopecode-dev" }),
    ...loopDefaults.owners.map((w) => loopIssue("owner-" + w, { about: w })),
    ...loopDefaults.not.map((l) => loopIssue("label-" + l, { labels: ["x", l] })),
    null
  ];
  expect(loopDoable(all).map((i) => i.id)).toEqual(["first", "a", "b"]);
  expect([loopDoable(null), loopDoable("x")]).toEqual([[], []]);
  return "3 of " + all.length;
}
// %%
test_loop_plan_is_the_table = {
  const p = (on, doable, machine, held = null) => loopPlan({ on, doable, machine, held }).do;
  expect([p(false, 3, "started"), p(false, 3, "stopped"), p(false, 0, null)]).toEqual(["down", null, null]);
  expect([p(true, 0, "stopped"), p(true, 0, "started"), p(true, 2, null), p(true, 2, "started"), p(true, 2, "starting"), p(true, 2, "stopped", "driver-x"), p(true, 2, "stopped")]).toEqual([null, null, null, null, null, null, "up"]);
  return "10 rows";
}
// %%
test_loop_a_push_starts_a_stopped_machine_for_work_and_nothing_else = {
  const rig = await loopRig({ issues: [loopIssue("w1")] });
  const r = await rig.call("receive");
  expect([r.status, r.data.on, r.data.last.did, r.data.last.doable, r.data.last.machine, rig.asked]).toEqual([200, true, "up", 1, "stopped", ["issue.list", "fly.status", "fly.up"]]);
  // Started: the next push does nothing.
  const again = await rig.call("receive");
  expect([again.data.last.did, again.data.last.why, rig.asked.length]).toEqual([null, "the machine is starting", 5]);
  // No work: nothing, and Fly is not asked to start.
  const idle = await loopRig({ issues: [loopIssue("r", { state: "in-review" })] });
  expect((await idle.call("check")).data.last).toMatchObject({ did: null, why: "no work", doable: 0 });
  expect(idle.asked).toEqual(["issue.list", "fly.status"]);
  // Off: a running machine is asked to yield, a stopped one is left.
  const off = await loopRig({ on: false, issues: [loopIssue("w1")], machine: "started" });
  expect((await off.call("receive")).data).toMatchObject({ on: false, last: { did: "down" } });
  const offStopped = await loopRig({ on: "false", issues: [loopIssue("w1")] });
  expect([(await offStopped.call("receive")).data.last.did, offStopped.asked.includes("fly.up")]).toEqual([null, false]);
  // The day's limit: Fly's refusal is the decision's error, and the call is still answered.
  const limit = await loopRig({ issues: [loopIssue("w1")], up: 409 });
  const l = (await limit.call("receive")).data.last;
  expect([l.did, typeof l.error, l.error.length > 0]).toEqual([null, "string", true]);
  return "up, nothing, down, refused";
}
// %%
test_loop_work_and_status_answer_the_list_and_the_last_decision = {
  const rig = await loopRig({ issues: [loopIssue("w2", { opened_at: 5, title: "x".repeat(300) }), loopIssue("w1"), loopIssue("not", { labels: ["laptop"] })] });
  const w = await rig.call("work");
  expect([w.status, w.data.work.map((i) => [i.id, i.about, i.title.length])]).toEqual([200, [["w1", "brain-x-git", 2], ["w2", "brain-x-git", 200]]]);
  expect((await rig.call("status")).data).toEqual({ on: true, last: null });
  await rig.call("check");
  expect(Object.keys((await rig.call("status")).data.last)).toEqual(["at", "by", "doable", "machine", "held", "did", "why", "error"]);
  // A verb that is not the method's, and a method that is not there.
  expect([(await rig.call("work", "POST")).status, (await rig.call("receive", "GET")).status, (await rig.call("run")).status]).toEqual([405, 405, 404]);
  return "work and status";
}
// %%
test_loop_declares_four_calls_no_cron_and_answers_the_owner_and_no_other = {
  const { meta } = await loop_service.emit();
  expect([meta.worker, meta.crons, meta.secrets]).toEqual(["brain-x-loop", [], []]);
  expect(meta.calls).toEqual(["com.lopecode.brain.fly.down", "com.lopecode.brain.fly.status", "com.lopecode.brain.fly.up", "com.lopecode.brain.issue.list"]);
  const may = (who) => decide({ allow: meta.access["com.lopecode.brain.loop.receive"].allow }, { caller: callerOf(who), origin: callerOf(who), request: { params: {} } }).allow;
  const callers = [{ caller: "owner", via: "session", tab: true }, { caller: "owner", via: "delegation:d1", holder: "worker:brain-x-topic", tab: false }, { caller: "owner", via: "delegation:d2", holder: "secret:fly-machine", tab: false }, { caller: "did:plc:member" }, { caller: "worker:brain-x-echo" }, { caller: "anonymous" }];
  expect(callers.map(may)).toEqual([true, true, true, false, false, false]);
  expect(Object.values(meta.access).every((a) => a.allow === 'caller.id == "owner"')).toBe(true);
  return Object.keys(meta.access).length + " methods";
}
// %%
import {cloudflare, rows, xrpc, config, log, simulate, decide, callerOf} from "@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac"
// %%
import {plugins} from "@tomlarkworthy/plugin-registry"
// %%
import {expect} from "@tomlarkworthy/jest-expect-standalone"
